From: 6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4 <6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:48:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gta4xl-common: sepolicy: Let the GNSS HAL find the sensor
 service

Samsung's GNSS HAL (vendor.samsung.hardware.gnss@2.0-service, loading
android.hardware.gnss@2.1-impl.so) dlopens libsensorndkbridge and calls
ASensorManager_getInstanceForPackage() to feed accelerometer/gyro data
to the GNSS firmware ("TGT_MEMS", gps.cfg: GlueLayer_IsMemsEnable=1,
Chip_Configuration_mems_data_Configuration=1 - MEMS static detection
and gyro heading estimation). Since Android 15 the bridge talks to the
AIDL android.frameworks.sensorservice.ISensorManager/default, which is
fwk_sensor_service, and nothing allows the HAL to find it:

  avc: denied { find } for pid=5426 uid=1000
  name=android.frameworks.sensorservice.ISensorManager/default
  scontext=u:r:hal_gnss_default:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:fwk_sensor_service:s0
  tclass=service_manager permissive=0

AServiceManager_waitForService() then fails (registerForNotifications
is refused as well), the HAL gets no ASensorManager and the MEMS
assistance silently stays off. Positioning itself keeps working; the
denial was already present on the lineage-23.2 baseline.

Add the same rule AOSP uses for hal_audio_default and hal_camera_default
("android.frameworks.sensorservice through libsensorndkbridge") and
Qualcomm's location daemons. Binder calls to/from system_server are
already covered by hal_gnss_client/hal_gnss_server.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sepolicy/vendor/hal_gnss_default.te | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/hal_gnss_default.te b/sepolicy/vendor/hal_gnss_default.te
index 6106c89..8c0d831 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/hal_gnss_default.te
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/hal_gnss_default.te
@@ -1 +1,5 @@
 allow hal_gnss_default gpsd:unix_stream_socket connectto;
+
+# android.frameworks.sensorservice through libsensorndkbridge
+# (android.hardware.gnss@2.1-impl.so, MEMS-assisted positioning)
+allow hal_gnss_default fwk_sensor_service:service_manager find;
